fact WorkItem(id: "WI-089", description: some(value: "anthill.realization.cpp_std: C++ language mapping file, sibling to rust_std.anthill. One LanguageMapping fact per profile (cpp17-stl, cpp20-stl) with effect_map (Modify to lvalue ref, Error to tl::expected wrap), type_map (Int to int64_t, Float to double, Bool to bool, String to std::string, List to std::vector, Option to std::optional, Bytes to std::vector of std::byte when WI-083 lands), trait_return TraitsClass per docs/cpp-forward-mapping.md. Plus a NamingConvention fact: language: cpp, method_case: camelCase, source_case: snake_case. Codegen uses this as the default when translating operation names. Per-operation overrides ride on WI-087 attributes (a CppName fact in the operation block) to handle irregulars such as acronyms (get_gps, get_imu). Value-level marshalling between anthill types and foreign host representations is an EXTENSION of this type_map, not a separate mechanism (WI-088): a TypeMapping entry gains an optional lift/lower adapter pair — entries with no adapter are the plain renames built here (Int -> int64_t, identity at the value level), entries with an adapter are marshalled (Vec3 -> `const double *`). The global cpp_std type_map built by THIS item carries only the identity renames; adapter-bearing entries are scoped to the foreign binding (the webots realization), per WI-088. WI-088 replaces the return-only ReturnTypeConversion placeholder currently in cpp_std. Driver: lf1 example needs cpp_std and lf1's webots realization references it."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-087"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-27T14:34:28Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "APPROACH (agreed in design discussion): make type-mapping lookup an ORDINARY KB QUERY, not a Rust reader. Retire hardcoded prim_lower/param_lower and do NOT add a TypeMapTable; the WI-088 MarshalTable is retired too (NO replacement reader). (1) KEYED ENTRIES (keys, NOT tags): every type mapping carries a single key that selects it. Renames keyed by profile (cpp17-stl/cpp20-stl); marshalling keyed by binding (webots). The key generalizes what profile already does (it IS the selector). Marshalling and renames are the SAME shape (TypeMapping with optional lift/lower), differing only by key and adapter-presence -- WI-088 one-concept thesis, finally uniform. (2) STANDARD QUERY: a relation lower_type(?keys, ?anthill_type, ?host, ?lift, ?lower) resolved by SLD against the keyed entries; cpp-gen calls kb.resolve(lower_type(active_keys, T, ...)) and reads host + adapters. The discrimination tree IS the table; the rule IS the overlay logic. This DELETES reader code instead of adding a third reader. (3) ACTIVE KEYS come from cpp-gen context, ordered most-specific-first. Always includes the compilation profile (Generated.profile). At a carrier-dispatch boundary, PREPEND the binding key, reusing NamespaceMapping.host_module (carrier sort namespace anthill.examples.lf1.webots -> host_module webots). So: declared-signature position (sort_to_cpp) uses active_keys=[profile] -> Vec3 misses -> generated struct (adapters invisible); carrier-boundary position (synthesise_body_for) uses active_keys=[binding, profile] -> Vec3 hits webots -> const double* + lift/lower. Boundary-only marshalling FALLS OUT of which keys are active where -- no special overlay rule. Carrier (global sort replacement via Implementation.carrier) stays an earlier, separate precedence step than the type-mapping query (it is a global replacement, not a boundary-only coercion). (4) PRIORITY is the only non-vanilla bit: binding-shadows-base = first-match over ordered keys. Encode either caller-side (cpp-gen tries keys in order, each query vanilla) or in-language (lower_type picks first key via member + NAF). Caller-side is simplest. OPEN FORK = entry representation: NESTED (keep renames in LanguageMapping.type_map + a key, project to a queryable relation via member(?type_map, TypeMapping(...)); VERIFY the resolver binds entity fields inside a list member) vs FLAT (top-level fact TypeMapping(key, anthill_type, host_type, lift, lower); more query-friendly, direct discrim hit, no list walk, but LanguageMapping no longer groups its type_map). Decide on whether member-over-list-entity-fields resolves cleanly. Also move INCLUDE_PROBES (host-type -> header) into the same keyed/queryable form, else fact-driven is half-done. WI-088 (depends on this) migrates the webots Vec3/EulerAngles entries to carry key webots and deletes MarshalTable.", at: "2026-06-25T12:45:11Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "ADDENDUM (predicate naming): the query predicates must be FULLY QUALIFIED. lower_type (and the projection relation, if the nested representation is used) live in anthill.realization -- the base realization namespace, sibling to LanguageMapping/TypeMapping/NamespaceMapping -- so every language mapping can use them. cpp-gen builds the query term with the full qualified name: kb.resolve(anthill.realization.lower_type(...)), matching how the existing reads resolve Implementation/TypeMapping via try_resolve_symbol(anthill.realization.X). Rationale: a bare short name is NOT scanned as a definition and would be interned as an unresolved symbol rather than resolving to the intended rule -- a silent mismatch. Full qualification keeps resolution unambiguous and consistent with the load.rs convention (all resolve_symbol calls use full paths).", at: "2026-06-25T12:45:15Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "CROSS-REF: cut (!) is now ticketed as WI-568 (kernel control primitive, proposal 033 §Future work / 033.1). It is the eventual clean form for the calculate_type_mapping priority -- TypeMapping(...)!, default instead of the NAF existence-wrapper. WI-089 does NOT depend on WI-568: ship on NAF (or caller-side first-match) now; adopt ! once WI-568 lands.", at: "2026-06-25T12:45:23Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "PROGRESS (increment landed, commit b2137d95; WI stays Claimed — full WI not yet delivered): the CORE type-map query is done, reviewed (/code-review, one finding fixed), green (cpp-gen 117/0, anthill-core clean). Delivered: (1) TypeMapping + lang/key Option fields; (2) cpp_std.anthill 10 flat keyed base renames (key=none = language base, all 6 fields explicit so arity-6 by construction); (3) cpp_base_host_type resolves host types via kb.query_view over an allocation-free Value::Entity pattern — ORDINARY KB QUERY, no reader / no TypeMapTable, works against cpp-gens immutable &KnowledgeBase (cannot kb.resolve / hash-cons); (4) prim_lower/param_lower deleted, 4 call sites rewired. DEFERRED follow-on increments: (a) profile threading + active-key priority + binding OVERLAYS — the WI-088 enabler (webots Vec3 -> key: some(webots)); (b) NamingConvention fact (camelCase) + effect_map facts (still hardcoded); (c) move INCLUDE_PROBES (host-type -> header) into the keyed/queryable form. Code-review notes judged acceptable: is_body_emittable leaf-widening (bare container unreachable), host_type continue (schema-required field), placeholder VarId scheme (query-side wildcards, bindings discarded).", at: "2026-06-25T13:40:57Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED + MERGED TO MAIN 2026-06-27 (merge 31d58bbf). Increments a+b+c all landed. (a) profile + binding active-key overlays + MarshalTable retirement = commit 19b53dc1; (b)/(c) effect_map + NamingConvention + INCLUDE_PROBES fact-driven = commit a4d89ad1. NET: cpp-gen reads ALL host mappings (types/effects/naming/includes/marshalling) from keyed facts via one query path with [binding?, profile?, none] active-key priority (binding overlay > profile overlay > language base); select_keyed/resolve_type_mapping is the single selector. MarshalTable retired (marshalling rides the same keyed TypeMapping query as renames). binding is an explicit Implementation.binding field (NOT host_module). profile threaded from Generated.profile via emit_namespace_header_with_profile. Tests green on the merged tree: cpp-gen 119/0, core/cli/stl 0 failed. /code-review high applied. CORRECTION (post-delivery): dropped the over-stated marshalling sharp-edge framing -- a TypeMapping not in the keyed cpp form is not malformed, just not selected; an unused fact is deleted at source, not guarded (commit d6ed629e). NOTE: the branch had filed WI-570 (cpp arrow-sort codegen) + WI-571 (capability gate) which COLLIDED with mains WI-502 reuse of those ids; re-filed under fresh ids post-merge.", at: "2026-06-27T14:34:33Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "CROSS-REF (2026-07-18, from WI-576): this ticket's ADDENDUM specified a fully-qualified anthill.realization.lower_type predicate resolved by SLD, with the overlay/priority logic IN the rule body. That did not ship and could not: cpp-gen holds a shared KB borrow and queries via kb.query_view, a discrimination-tree HEAD MATCH that never runs a rule body, while SLD needs a mutable KB (it allocs/interns). So the delivered form is the Rust query_type_mappings + select_keyed pair, and lower_type exists nowhere in stdlib/. WI-576's realizes_effect accessor hit the identical wall and made the identical choice. The enabling substrate change is now tracked as WI-760 (codegen gets a resolving KnowledgeBase); it also records the trap that writing lower_type as a BODIED rule TODAY would head-match with its body silently unevaluated.", at: "2026-07-18T14:58:17Z")
